Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments (ACME)
on the International Space Station (ISS)
Tests carried out within the
Combustion Integrated Rack (CIR).
Hardware set up by ISS crew members
from Canada, Germany, Italy, Japan,
Russia, and the United States
Tests remotely commanded from
NASA's Glenn ISS Payload Operations
Center.
Four CIR ground consoles staffed
during test operations.
Laminar spherical and axisymmetric nonpremixed
flames of gaseous fuels.
Fundamental research focused primarily on practical
terrestrial combustion, but also spacecraft fire safety.
Six independent experiments using one set of modular
hardware.
Five studies selected by NASA. One study selected
by NSF (National Science Foundation) and CASIS
(Center for the Advancement of Science in Spacе).
